{
  "action": "In general, a standard system update will make all the necessary changes.",
  "cves": [
    "CVE-2026-63388",
    "CVE-2026-63387"
  ],
  "description": "Micha\u0142 Majchrowicz and Marcin Wyczechowski discovered that libevent\nincorrectly handled certain DNS responses. A remote attacker could possibly\nuse this issue to cause a denial of service or execute arbitrary code.\n(CVE-2026-63387)\n\nIt was discovered that libevent incorrectly handled certain connections. A\nlocal attacker could possibly use this issue to cause a denial of service\nor execute arbitrary code. This issue only affected Ubuntu 18.04 LTS,\nUbuntu 20.04 LTS, Ubuntu 22.04 LTS, Ubuntu 24.04 LTS, and Ubuntu 26.04 LTS.\n(CVE-2026-63388)",
  "id": "USN-8840-1",
  "isummary": "Several security issues were fixed in libevent.",
